From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhzy0077 <zhzy0077@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: restore audio after reconnect with active video

A brief HPD drop clears the audio jack, but the following connection can
leave the video stream enabled without another atomic enable. The audio
jack then remains disconnected. This also occurs with external HPD
bridges, which do not report ISR_HPD_REPLUG_COUNT in the hardware status.

On Gaokun3, tracing captured a USB-C HPD disconnect followed 758 ms later
by a connection, with video still active and no post-enable callback.
ALSA retained a disconnected DP0 jack despite the connected display.

After a successful connection, refresh post-enable state when the video
stream is already powered on. This restores audio link parameters and
the jack notification. New streams use the normal atomic-enable path.

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -1558,13 +1558,15 @@
 		   msm_dp_display->connector_type, hpd_link_status, status);
 
 	if (status == connector_status_connected) {
-		if (hpd_link_status == ISR_HPD_REPLUG_COUNT) {
-			msm_dp_hpd_unplug_handle(dp);
-			msm_dp_hpd_plug_handle(dp);
-		} else if (hpd_link_status == ISR_IRQ_HPD_PULSE_COUNT) {
+		if (hpd_link_status == ISR_IRQ_HPD_PULSE_COUNT) {
 			msm_dp_irq_hpd_handle(dp);
 		} else {
-			msm_dp_hpd_plug_handle(dp);
+			if (hpd_link_status == ISR_HPD_REPLUG_COUNT)
+				msm_dp_hpd_unplug_handle(dp);
+
+			/* A brief HPD drop can leave the video stream enabled. */
+			if (!msm_dp_hpd_plug_handle(dp) && msm_dp_display->power_on)
+				msm_dp_display_post_enable(msm_dp_display);
 		}
 	} else {
 		msm_dp_hpd_unplug_handle(dp);
